Session management

Because the site is static, there is no secure server-side session by default.

Implement the safest practical browser-only behavior:

- Default to session-only token storage.
- Use "sessionStorage" for temporary sessions where appropriate.
- If Remember Me is selected, clearly explain that persistent browser storage exposes the token to JavaScript executing in the same origin.
- Require explicit consent before persisting a token.
- Provide a visible Logout button.
- Clear the token and related authentication state on logout.
- Never store tokens in the project registry or other public website data.
- Never transmit a token to any service other than the intended GitHub API origin.
- Do not send tokens to analytics, third-party scripts, or external image hosts.

Do not claim that "localStorage" encryption makes a client-side token secure against malicious same-origin JavaScript.

If secure persistent authentication is required, explain the need for a server-side authentication component rather than pretending that static hosting can provide secure server sessions.

